  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Indra Air Traffic has $384M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 26 awards with an average award size of $14.8M. Obligations are up 160.7% year over year. Obligations rose from $0 in FY21 and FY22 to $104K in FY23, then $16.8M in FY24, $147M in FY25, and $384M in FY26. The Department of Transportation is the dominant buyer, obligating $383M. The Department of Defense obligated $815K. The largest market is Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing with $378M. Other markets with recorded obligations include Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $3M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services with $2.5M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations rose 160.7% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations moved from $104K in FY23 to $16.8M in FY24, $147M in FY25, and $384M in FY26. The FY21 and FY22 obligations were $0 for both years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets do they fund?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $383M and the Department of Defense obligated $815K in FY2026 to date. The largest market is Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing with $378M, followed by Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $3M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services with $2.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
